            <ArticleTitle>[A case of Churg-Strauss syndrome undergoing cesarean section].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>420-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 37-year-old woman with Churg-Strauss syndrome underwent cesarean section under combined spinal-epidural anesthesia. Churg-Strauss syndrome is a rare diffuse vasculitis accompanied by severe asthma. Anesthesia was performed uneventfully, but there were several issues of concern regarding the perioperative management of this syndrome.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
